{%- comment -%}
  ─── THE PHOTO GRID ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The browsing surface. Everything in the current collection, listed, as
  photographs. Replaces Dawn's `main-collection-product-grid` on the collection
  template.

  IT IS SERVER-RENDERED AND PAGINATED, which is what makes the quick view safe:
  the address bar can carry a real product URL because there is a real product
  page behind it, and a crawler walking this grid finds ordinary <a> links to
  ordinary pages. Nothing here is a single-page app.

  IT ALSO SERVES TAG-FILTERED URLS. Shopify applies /collections/all/{tag} to
  `collection.products` before the template runs, so this same section renders
  /collections/sneakers and /collections/all/tracksuits-sets identically without
  knowing which it is. That is what lets the navigation address the whole
  catalogue by tag (see snippets/marathon-nav.liquid for why it must).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- render 'marathon-identity' -%}

{%- render 'marathon-nav' -%}

{%- liquid
  assign here = collection.current_tags.first
  assign all_tags = collections.all.all_tags
  assign footwear = 'Sneakers,Boots,Sandals & Slides,Soccer Boots' | split: ','
  assign everything_else = 'Tracksuits & Sets,Caps & Hats,Jerseys,Polos,Jeans & Denim,Jackets & Coats,Hoodies & Sweatshirts,T-Shirts,Shorts & Vests,Bags,Perfume' | split: ','

  # The sibling strip shows the categories a shopper would move to NEXT, which
  # for a shoe is the other shoes. Anything else gets the general row.
  assign siblings = everything_else
  if footwear contains here
    assign siblings = footwear
  endif
-%}

<div class="page-width mc-page">
  <header class="mc-head">
    <h1 class="mc-head__title">
      {%- if here != blank -%}
        {{ collection.current_tags | join: ' · ' }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ collection.title | default: 'Everything' }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </h1>
    <p class="mc-head__count">
      {{ collection.products_count }} {% if collection.products_count == 1 %}item{% else %}items{% endif %}
    </p>
  </header>

  {%- comment -%}
    ─── SORT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    LINKS, NOT A SELECT. A `<select>` needs JavaScript to submit on change, and
    a submit button next to it is a second control for one decision. Three links
    are server-rendered, work with JavaScript off, are crawlable, and are quiet
    enough to sit under the heading without competing with the photographs.

    THE OPTIONS ARE DELIBERATELY THREE. Shopify offers seven; four of them are
    useless or misleading on this catalogue:
      • title A-Z / Z-A — the names are machine-generated and carry no brand, so
        alphabetical order is noise ("Sneaker Audysol…" tells a shopper nothing).
      • best-selling — Shopify counts ONLINE sales, and this storefront is new
        and barely visited. It would rank noise and look authoritative doing it.
        (What actually sells is measured from the tills instead, and drives the
        home page — see sections/marathon-home.liquid.)
      • manual — no collection here has a hand-ordered sequence to respect.
    Newest and the two price directions are the three a shopper can actually use.

    `sort_by` works on tag-addressed URLs as well as collection URLs — verified
    against production 2026-08-21 on /collections/all/tracksuits-sets, where
    price-ascending and price-descending return different first products.
    Deliberately NOT carrying `page`: changing the sort must return to page 1.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign active_sort = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by
    assign sorts = 'created-descending|Newest,price-ascending|Price low to high,price-descending|Price high to low' | split: ','

    # The page's own address, rebuilt from the collection rather than read from
    # `request.path`. On a tag-filtered page `collection.url` is /collections/all
    # and the tag is the segment after it, so the two together ARE the address —
    # and they come from the objects this template already has rather than from
    # a separate request drop that could disagree with them.
    assign sort_base = collection.url
    if here != blank
      assign sort_base = here | handleize | prepend: '/' | prepend: collection.url
    endif
  -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    IF THE PAGE IS IN AN ORDER THIS CONTROL DOES NOT OFFER, IT SAYS SO.
    A shopper arriving from a search engine on a bare /collections/all/{tag} gets
    Shopify's title-ascending default, which is none of the three below. Showing
    three links with none of them marked leaves the shopper unable to tell what
    order they are looking at — so the actual order is rendered as a fourth,
    current-marked entry instead. Honest about the state, and one tap from a
    useful one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign offered = 'created-descending,price-ascending,price-descending' | split: ','
    assign active_is_offered = false
    if offered contains active_sort
      assign active_is_offered = true
    endif
    assign other_labels = 'title-ascending|A to Z,title-descending|Z to A,best-selling|Best selling,manual|Featured,created-ascending|Oldest' | split: ','
    assign active_label = ''
    for row in other_labels
      assign kv = row | split: '|'
      if kv[0] == active_sort
        assign active_label = kv[1]
      endif
    endfor
  -%}
  {%- if collection.products_count > 1 -%}
    <div class="mc-sort">
      <span class="mc-sort__label">Sort</span>
      {%- unless active_is_offered -%}
        {%- if active_label != blank -%}
          <span class="mc-sort__link" aria-current="true">{{ active_label }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
      {%- for s in sorts -%}
        {%- assign bits = s | split: '|' -%}
        <a class="mc-sort__link"
           href="{{ sort_base }}?sort_by={{ bits[0] }}"
           {% if active_sort == bits[0] %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>{{ bits[1] }}</a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    THE SIBLING STRIP — "where else can I go", stated rather than hidden behind
    a dropdown. Every entry is checked against `all_tags`, so it can never offer
    a dead end.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if here != blank -%}
    <div class="mc-siblings">
      {%- for s in siblings -%}
        {%- if all_tags contains s -%}
          {%- comment -%} Newest-first, for the reason set out in
            snippets/marathon-nav.liquid: a tag URL inherits collections.all's
            title-ascending default, which sorts machine-generated names
            alphabetically and is the one ordering worth nothing here. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign sib = s | handleize | prepend: '/collections/all/' | append: '?sort_by=created-descending' -%}
          <a href="{{ sib }}"
             {% if s == here %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ s }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- paginate collection.products by section.settings.per_page -%}
    {%- if collection.products.size == 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Degrade rather than break. A category that has sold out says so in a
        sentence and offers the way back, instead of rendering an empty grid.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="mc-empty">
        Nothing in this section right now.
        <a href="/collections/all?sort_by=created-descending">See everything</a>.
      </p>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="mc-grid">
        {%- for product in collection.products -%}
          {%- comment -%} The first row is eager. Five, not two: the grid is
            five columns at >=1400px, and a lazy card in the opening row renders
            as an empty frame until the scroll handler fires. Below that width
            the extra eager images are still above or just below the fold.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign lazy = 'lazy' -%}
          {%- if forloop.index <= 5 -%}{%- assign lazy = 'eager' -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- render 'marathon-card', product: product, lazy: lazy -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
        {{ paginate | default_pagination }}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endpaginate -%}
</div>

<script src="{{ 'marathon-storefront.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Photo grid",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "per_page",
      "min": 12,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 4,
      "default": 24,
      "label": "Products per page"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Photo grid" }]
}
{% endschema %}
